1. e4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. Nc3 a6 $5 {Black is trying to go ...b7-b5 before ...d7-d6, which is not an entirely stupid idea. However, there are some drawbacks, which we will soon see.} 4. Be3 b5 (4... d6 {transposes back to the main line.}) 5. h4 $1 {In the main line, I recommended g2-g4, which is easier to play than h2-h4, but here we have a favorable version of the h2-h4 mainline. Because Black does not have ...d7-d6 yet, Black's main idea against what we're about to do does not work.} h5 {In general, this would be the move I would want to avoid and the reason we go for g2-g4 first in the main line. But here, there is an important difference on display.} 6. Nf3 $1 {[%cal Gf3g5] Rushing to g5.} d6 {This is probably best, but hardly inspiring.} 7. Ng5 $1 Nf6 8. Bd3 $16 {We are very happy to have the knight posted up on g5. e5 hangs over Black's head like the sword of Damocles, and compared to a normal Modern, we have not had to spend on tempo on f2-f3 to protect e4 or keep the knight off of g4.} *

