1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 ({Now, anything other than} 3. Nc3 dxe4 {would be quite surprising. Still, it's good to have some sense of what to do if Black tried to mix things up.}) 3... g6 4. e5 Bg7 {Now, all White needs to know is not to rush with f2-f4. This will give Black the Gurgenidze setup, which is not that easy to break down.} 5. h3 $1 {This seems quite sufficient. White wants Nf3 next without running into ...Bg4.} Nh6 6. g4 $1 O-O 7. f4 $1 {Again, no Gurgenidze for you.} *

[Event "Lifetime Repertoires: Shankland's 1.e4 – Part 1 Caro-Kann, French & Sidelines"]
[Site "?"]
