1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 dxe4 {The Rubinstein French has never been that popular, but it's a tough nut to crack. Black's position is definitely under pressure and there are a lot of lines to know for them, but it's not like he is automatically crushed or anything.In my own experience, I have had trouble showing much of anything the few times it has been played against me. That said, for this course, I found some stuff that I liked.} 4. Nxe4 ({Now, Black's main move by far is} 4. Nxe4 Nd7 {, with the plan of playing} 5. Z0 Ngf6 {next. But there are some extraneous options that White should be aware of.}) 4... Nd7 5. Nf3 Ngf6 6. Nxf6+ {Much like we saw in the Caro, I often want to resolve the tension as soon as possible on f6.} Nxf6 7. Bd3 {Now, I like that Black gets a very dangerous position if they continue with ...Be7 and ...O-O, which looks the most natural if someone is freestyling. They are provoked into a confrontation right away.} c5 $1 8. Be3 Qc7 9. Qe2 a6 ({This is Black's main move, stopping any hopes of a check on b5, and they want to go} 9... a6 10. Z0 Nd5 {next. Now, I like a modern computer move to put his position under more pressure.}) 10. h4 $5 ({In a funny way, this is kind of a waiting move. The point is that if we were to castle long,} 10. O-O-O {, Black could immediately play} b5 {without worrying about a2-a4.Now, ...b7-b5 would allow the queenside to become compromised. But what else does Black do? ...Be7 gives us the tempo we want.}) 10... Bd7 {This was Ferenc Berkes's choice in the only GM game to reach this position. Given how well they matched the machine in the upcoming moves, I am very confident this was preparation, and I do think it is best. But I also think that White can put Black under a lot of pressure.} 11. O-O-O $1 {Now and only now, we castle long. Black can still play ...b7-b5, but then they do not get their bishop to b7.} Rc8 $1 12. Ne5 Ba4 $1 {Black's point is that the bishop is quite annoying on a4, and that if we ever push b2-b3, ...Nf6-d5 comes and we will regret weakening the c3-square.} 13. h5 Nd5 14. Rd2 $14 {Overprotecting c2 so that the queen can get to g4. Black definitely still has some problems to solve here.} *

