[Black "French Steinitz Sidelines #1"]
[Result "*"]
[ECO "C11"]
[Annotator "SchackNuva"]
[PlyCount "23"]
[GameId "2288537760555105"]

1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Nf6 {The Steinitz is one of Black's two main tries after Nc3. In general, I think it is a more promising option for them than the Winawer because they do not lose the dark-squared bishop.} 4. e5 Nfd7 ({Now, in recent times,} 4... Nfd7 5. Nce2 {has been gaining some popularity.} ({I even played it myself the last time I faced the Steinitz, winning a nice game against Ray Robson.However, I ultimately think that the main line with} 5. f4 {is a much more testing way of playing, and I was happy to have an opportunity to dig deep while writing this course.})) 5. f4 c5 {Anything else would be utterly shocking.} 6. Nf3 Be7 {This move is unlikely to have independent value, but if Black wants a plan with ...b7-b6, this is the best move order.} 7. Be3 b6 ({Now, at least Black is not immediately smashed by ...f7-f5. But they are definitely still worse.} 7... Nc6 {transposes to the mainline with 7...Be7.}) 8. Ne2 $1 {I find that a good rule of thumb is that whenever Black plays ...a7-a6, ...b7-b6, or some move that generally does not contest the center, it tends to be a good idea to follow up with Nc3-e2.Nce2 is a very good coordination for White, but it can run into concrete issues with ...Qb6 and attacking the center. Once Black plays a move that does not mesh well with a direct central assault, Nc3-e2 makes a lot of sense.} Ba6 9. c3 Nc6 10. h4 {As usual, once we play with Nce2, the best plan will be to go for h2-h4 next to gain kingside space.} O-O $6 11. Ng5 $1 {This move is quite annoying for Black to deal with. They will never be able to push ...f7-f6 thanks to the weakness on e6, but then what else can they do? We never have to worry about ...h7-h6.} Re8 ({This was my best attempt at finding a human move for Black. They can hope for} 11... Re8 12. Z0 Nf8 {next to overprotect h7 and e6, and then at some point, they can play ...f7-f6.}) 12. Kf2 $16 {Black is completely devoid of active ideas, and even if ...Nf8 and ...f7-f6 come, simply Nf3 back is fine. White can continue gaining more kingside space with g2-g4 next.} *

