1. e4 g5 $2 ({If you are playing online, I would suspect this move is a mouseslip, as} 1... g6 {is a much more serious option.}) 2. d4 g4 3. Nc3 ({Don't bother dealing with the complications after} 3. Qxg4 d5 {. Simple development is sufficient to secure a winning advantage. After all, what exactly has Black accomplished by rushing the g-pawn?}) 3... Bg7 4. Be3 $18 {[%cal Gh2h3,Gd1d2,Ge1c1] Later, we can start chipping away at the g4-pawn with moves like h2-h3 and f2-f3. If we are successful in forcing a trade, it will be a huge tempo blow for Black, since they wasted three tempi to capture a pawn that only moved once.} *

