1. e4 b5 $2 {It isn't that deep, there's really not too much to look at here.} 2. Bxb5 {White can and should take the pawn.} Bb7 {[%cal Ga4e8,Rd7d5]} (2... c6 3. Ba4 {is still not allowing ...d7-d5} Nf6 4. Nc3 $18 {.}) 3. Nc3 f5 {[%csl Re4]} 4. d3 $18 {[%csl Ge4][%cal Gd1e2] It is over, White is up a pawn for nothing. Next up, we can play Qe2 and further protect the e4-pawn, then develop routinely.} *

