1. e4 f5 $4 {The worst move Black can play on move one, and the only one where White is winning right off the bat. Therefore, we should try to do our worst.} 2. exf5 {[%cal Gd1h5]} Nf6 {Otherwise a check on h5 causes even more problems.} 3. d4 d5 {[%csl Rf5] I can't imagine anything else coming.} 4. Bd3 ({Black has three options: play} 4. Bd3 e6 ({immediately, play} 4... c5 {first, then ...e7-e6, or play}) (4... Nc6 {then ...e7-e6.})) 4... Nc6 {[%csl Rd4]} 5. Nf3 Nb4 {Taking the bishop won't help Black get the pawn back:} 6. O-O Nxd3 7. Qxd3 Qd7 {[%csl Rf5]} 8. Nh4 $18 {[%csl Rf8,Gf5] We remain a clean pawn up, and Black cannot develop the f8-bishop.} *

