1. e4 f5 $4 {The worst move Black can play on move one, and the only one where White is winning right off the bat. Therefore, we should try to do our worst.} 2. exf5 {[%cal Gd1h5]} Nf6 {Otherwise a check on h5 causes even more problems.} 3. d4 d5 {[%csl Rf5] I can't imagine anything else coming.} 4. Bd3 ({Black has three options: play} 4. Bd3 e6 ({immediately, play} 4... c5 {first, then ...e7-e6, or play}) (4... Nc6 {then ...e7-e6.})) 4... c5 {[%csl Rf5][%cal Gc5c4,Bc8f5] Black is threatening to play ...c5-c4 and drive away the bishop.} 5. c3 {[%csl Gc2][%cal Gd3c2] We make room for the bishop while simultaneously protecting d4.} cxd4 6. Nf3 $1 {This is more incisive than capturing back right away. We want to take on d4 with the knight to preserve our structure and make it harder for Black to play ...e7-e6.} (6. cxd4 $6 {at least allows the pawn to be isolated.}) 6... dxc3 7. Nxc3 {White is almost +3 here. Black gambited a pawn, only to be behind in development.} *

