1. e4 f5 $4 {The worst move Black can play on move one, and the only one where White is winning right off the bat. Therefore, we should try to do our worst.} 2. exf5 {[%cal Gd1h5]} Nf6 {Otherwise a check on h5 causes even more problems.} 3. d4 d5 {[%csl Rf5] I can't imagine anything else coming.} 4. Bd3 ({Black has three options: play} 4. Bd3 e6 ({immediately, play} 4... c5 {first, then ...e7-e6, or play}) (4... Nc6 {then ...e7-e6.})) 4... c5 {[%csl Rf5][%cal Gc5c4,Bc8f5] Black is threatening to play ...c5-c4 and drive away the bishop.} 5. c3 {[%csl Gc2][%cal Gd3c2] We make room for the bishop while simultaneously protecting d4.} e6 (5... Nc6 6. Nf3 {should transpose to some version of ...e7-e6. Black really can't avoid playing ...e7-e6, or he can't develop their bishop.}) 6. fxe6 Bxe6 7. Qe2 {[%csl Re6]} Qe7 8. dxc5 $18 {[%csl Re6][%cal Re7c5] White is two pawns up, and totally winning.} *

