1. e4 f6 $2 {This one is also very bad. Black opens up their king and messes up their development.} 2. d4 e5 3. dxe5 $18 {[%csl Re5][%cal Rf6e5,Rd1h5,Rh5e5,Rh5e8]} ({Black loses a pawn for nothing; recapturing,} 3. dxe5 fxe5 {, will result in a quick capitulation after} 4. Qh5+ $18 {.}) 3... Nc6 {The best move in a bad position.} 4. Nf3 {There is no reason to take on f6 and allow Black to accelerate their development.} fxe5 5. Bc4 $18 {[%cal Ga2g8,Gf3g5] White is already winning thanks to his pressure on the a2-g8 diagonal. Black will not be able to castle, and moves like Ng5 are already looking problematic.We will see later in the 1...e5 course that White sometimes gets a position like this one a full tempo down in the Schliemann, and even then, Black is notably worse. Now, they are busted.} *

