1. e4 f6 $2 {This one is also very bad. Black opens up their king and messes up their development.} 2. d4 e6 (2... g6 {transposes to the 1...Nh6 lines after the typical developers Nc3 & Be3 and ...Nh6 & ...Bg7.}) 3. Ne2 $16 {[%csl Ye6][%cal Gb1c3,Ge2f4,Rd1h5,Yd5e6,Yd7e6,Gd4d5] I like this development scheme. The one benefit that ...f7-f6 does have is that it restricts a knight on f3. Instead, we develop this knight to e2, and prepare to place it on f4. Next up, we use the d5-pawn as a battering ram against the e6-pawn, which will help us blow up the center.} *

