1. e4 h5 2. d4 h4 {Against other moves, we can proceed with typical development. With the white king castling kingside, Black players often opt for ...h5-h4 and try to play ...h4-h3 with some hopes for play along the h-file. We can shut this down real fast with the simple:} 3. h3 $16 {[%csl Gh3][%cal Gc2c4,Gb1c3,Gg1f3] When Black's entire plan is foiled. This time, we develop with the three pawns c-d-e, to avoid weakening the g3-square, followed by usual development.The h4-pawn will likely prove to be a liability in the future.} *

