1. e4 h6 ({This is significantly worse than its counterpart} 1... a6 {, since following up with ...b7-b5 is a much more viable idea than ...g7-g5, which weakens the side the king is more likely to castle to. Thus, we can safely play Nf3 without worrying about ...g5-g4.}) 2. d4 g5 $6 {Stubbornly forging ahead with this idea anyways.} 3. h4 {[%csl Rg5] Another difference with ...a7-a6 & ...b7-b5 is that there is no ...Bg7 here, since d4 is protected.} g4 4. Nc3 $18 {[%csl Yf4,Yf5,Rg4,Yh5] Don't be tempted by the pawn. Black is positionally busted, their position lagging in development, and riddled with tons of weaknesses.} *

