1. e4 h6 ({This is significantly worse than its counterpart} 1... a6 {, since following up with ...b7-b5 is a much more viable idea than ...g7-g5, which weakens the side the king is more likely to castle to. Thus, we can safely play Nf3 without worrying about ...g5-g4.}) 2. d4 c6 ({▷} 2... a6 {If someone plays this, they have to be trolling. In no universe does this make sense.} 3. c4 $16 {Three pawns in the center, then develop. There's nothing to show for Black.}) ({▷} 2... e6 3. Bd3 d5 4. Nc3 {Transposes to the ...h7-h6 French sideline.}) 3. Bd3 d5 4. e5 $16 {[%csl Rh6][%cal Rc8f5] ...is a very poor advance Caro. Black now can't play the bishop to f5, which is one of the main ideas of the whole opening, and also ...h7-h6 weakens the kingside.} *

