1. e4 Nh6 $2 {There are two ways Black usually plays this: The more traditional way is the plan of playing a system with ...g7-g6, ...f7-f6 and ...Nf7, and the more modern interpretation is trying to play ...d7-d5 and clear the f5-square for the knight.} 2. d4 d5 3. exd5 Qxd5 4. Nc3 {[%csl Rd5]} Qd8 5. Nf3 $1 Nf5 {The only way to justify the whole opening.} 6. Bf4 e6 7. Qd2 $18 {[%csl Ra8,Rb8,Rc8,Rd8,Re8,Rf8,Rh8] The knight on f5 is not bad, but Black has lost way too much time and space getting it there. White should be winning due to the huge lead in development.} *

