1. e4 Nc6 2. d4 d5 3. e5 Bf5 4. c3 e6 5. Nd2 f6 6. f4 g5 7. Ndf3 fxe5 $2 (7... gxf4 {here is the main move for Black.}) ({As we covered,} 7... fxe5 {is a serious error, since Black needs to make White take with the d-pawn to alleviate the space deficit.}) 8. Nxe5 $1 {[%cal Rg5g4] We don't want to allow ...g5-g4, so we trade knights before fxe5.} Nxe5 9. fxe5 g4 $6 (9... Qe7 {should be tried. Black needs to get developed as quickly as possible.} 10. Bd3 Bxd3 11. Qxd3 O-O-O 12. Ne2 Qg7 $1 13. h4 Be7 {, and Black is starting to untangle, but White is still clearly in the driver's seat}) 10. Bd3 {[%csl Gd3,Rf5] Eliminating the roadblock on the f-file} Bxd3 11. Qxd3 {You can train the line here.} Qd7 12. Ne2 O-O-O 13. O-O $18 {[%csl Rf8,Rg8,Rh8][%cal Gf1f8] It's already over. White will soon dominate the f-file, and the remaining Black minors have trouble getting out.} h5 $6 {This move accelerates the end, there was no reason to weaken the g6-square and allow the queen to infiltrate...} 14. Qg6 Bh6 15. Rf7 Qe8 16. Bf4 Rd7 17. Rg7 Qf8 18. Rxg8 $1 {From here, the rest of the game is really just a formality.} Rxg8 19. Qxh6 Qe8 20. Bg3 Rh8 21. Qg5 Rf7 22. Bh4 Qb5 23. Qd2 Rhh7 24. Nf4 Qc6 25. Rf1 b6 26. b3 Kb7 27. Qd3 Rf5 28. Bf6 h4 29. Nxe6 Rxf1+ 30. Kxf1 Qxe6 31. Qxh7 g3 32. hxg3 hxg3 33. Qg6 a5 34. a4 c5 35. Ke2 cxd4 36. cxd4 Qc6 37. Kd2 b5 38. axb5 Qxb5 39. Qxg3 a4 40. bxa4 Qb2+ 41. Ke3 Qc3+ 42. Kf4 Qxd4+ 43. Kf5 Qe4+ 44. Ke6 d4 45. Qf3 1-0

