1. e4 Nc6 2. d4 e5 3. d5 Nce7 4. Nf3 Ng6 5. h4 h5 6. Bg5 Nf6 7. Nc3 Be7 8. Bxf6 Bxf6 9. d6 $1 {Immediately jacking up Black's pawn structure. You will see just how annoying this really is.} c6 10. g3 Nf8 $1 {[%cal Gf8e6,Ge6c5] Black's only hope is to bring the g6-knight back into the game via e6 and c5.} 11. Qd2 {You can follow the line here.} Ne6 12. Bh3 b6 13. O-O-O a5 14. Kb1 (14. Bxe6 $1 {is the thematic idea, removing Black's only good piece for our bad bishop.} dxe6 15. Kb1 Bd7 {It looks like Black is alive, but after} 16. g4 $18 {it turns out that it's all an illusion.The rooks are not able to communicate on the back rank when the kingside files open up. The d6-pawn remains a gigantic asset, keeping the pieces pinned down in the center.}) 14... Ra7 15. Ne2 Nc5 16. Qe3 Kf8 17. Nc1 a4 18. a3 Ra5 19. Ng5 Ba6 ({Here for some reason, Hall begins losing the thread and making strange moves.Any of the top three most reasonable moves at a first glance are winning:} 19... Ba6 20. Rhe1 ({,} 20. f4) ({, even} 20. Na2 {.}) ({I'm not sure what the point of} 20. Rh2 {was.})) 20. Rh2 $6 Qe8 21. Re1 $6 Nb7 $1 {Tony Miles is certainly resourceful. Now White's job is not so easy.} 22. Rd1 {The rook has to go back, wasting two tempi.} Rh6 23. f4 Bxg5 24. fxg5 $6 (24. hxg5 $1 Rxd6 25. Rdh1 {White is crashing through on the h-file.}) 24... Rxd6 25. Rxd6 Nxd6 26. Qxb6 Nc4 27. Qb4+ c5 28. Qc3 {By this point, the swindle has been complete. Unfortunately, Black's job practically is still not so simple and Miles fails to save it from here.} Qd8 $2 (28... Qa8 $1 {, activating the queen, and preparing to make threats against the White monarch along the b-file is enough to equalize the game.}) 29. Rf2 Rb5 30. Nd3 Rb8 $4 {[%csl Rc5,Re5]} ({Blunders a pawn.} 30... Qc7 {, defending e5, is required.}) 31. Nxe5 Nxe5 32. Qxe5 d6 33. Qf5 Bc4 34. Bf1 Qb6 35. c3 Qb5 36. Bxc4 Qxc4 37. g6 f6 38. Qd5 Qxd5 39. exd5 $18 {[%csl Ra4,Rh5][%cal Gf2f5,Gf2f4] The rook endgame is hopeless. White is up a pawn and there are way too many weaknesses on top of that.} Ke7 40. Re2+ Kd7 41. Re4 Ra8 42. Kc2 Kd8 43. Kd3 Kd7 44. Rf4 Ke7 45. Ke3 Kd7 46. Kf3 Kc7 47. Re4 Kd7 48. Kf4 Ra5 49. g4 hxg4 50. Kxg4 c4 51. Rxc4 Rxd5 52. Rxa4 Rd2 53. Ra7+ Ke6 54. Rxg7 Rxb2 55. h5 Rg2+ 56. Kf3 Rh2 57. Rh7 Rh3+ 58. Kg2 Rxc3 59. Ra7 Rc5 60. g7 Rxh5 1-0

