1. e4 Nc6 2. d4 d6 $6 {A few fanatic defenders of this line exist, like Kostya Kavutskiy, but if there is one thing I am going to drill into your mind, it's going to be the value of space. Modern engines all consider space as one of the most important factors.That's why most of these sidelines that dilly dally on the flanks are borderline unplayable.} 3. d5 $1 {[%csl Rc6] Usually, the downside with gaining space is that you are losing time, so you will fall behind in development and the pawns may become overextended. However, Black has conveniently fixed this problem for us by allowing us to gain time and space at the same time!} Ne5 {This refuses to admit defeat and instead invites White to kick the knight around a few more times.} 4. f4 {[%csl Re5]} Nd7 {[%csl Rg6][%cal Bg7g6,Bf8g7]} (4... Ng6 $2 {just causes a traffic jam on the kingside. The bishop can't develop properly.} 5. Nc3 $18) 5. Nf3 c6 6. c4 $16 {[%csl Gc4,Gd5,Ge4,Gf4] Since Black has given up all the space and gotten nothing in return, we can confidently evaluate this as being a clear opening success.} *

