[White "3) Nimzowitsch with 2...d5"]
[Black "3B | 5...f6 6.f4 Nh6 #2"]
[Result "*"]
[ECO "B00"]
[Annotator "SchackNuva"]
[PlyCount "21"]
[GameId "2288537760833700"]

1. e4 Nc6 2. d4 d5 {[%cal Bc8f5,Be7e6,Bf7f6,Bd8d7,Be8c8,Ge4e5,Gc2c3,Gf2f4]} ({By far the best continuation after 2.d4. The idea is that after} 2... d5 3. exd5 Qxd5 {, White is not in time for} 4. Nc3 {since d4 is under attack, and Black seizes the initiative in a vastly improved Scandi. The best continuation for us is 3.e5, grabbing space and getting a position similar to the Advance French and Caro lines.The advantage ...Nc6 gives over the other two is that the development of the bishop and knight are not compromised ...c7-c6 blocks the knight, ...e7-e6 blocks the bishop, and subsequently Black's piece development will be much more harmonious.However, it also comes with a major drawback: Black is no longer able to play ...c7-c5 to strike the base of the pawn chain. This means that to challenge the center, Black's plan will now be to attack the chain from the head with a plan revolving around ...f7-f6. Knowing this, we can determine that the optimal setup for Black will be ...Bf5, ...e7-e6, ...f7-f6, ...Qd7, and ...O-O-O. If we have to recapture on e5 with the d-pawn, then Black will coordinate with ...Bc5 and ...Nge7 with too much activity.Thus, White's best setups are all connected with f2-f4, in order to recapture on e5 with the f-pawn instead.}) 3. e5 Bf5 4. c3 e6 5. Nd2 {[%csl Re4][%cal Gd2f3,Yd2e4] Many players have tried Bd3 instead of Nd2, to trade off the active bishop. However, I believe White can try to exploit the f5-bishop's position with h2-h4 and g2-g4, so we should not jump to trade it off.Nd2 here takes control of the e4-square from the bishop, so we are ready for f2-f4 and g2-g4 without Be4 happening. Here, Black's most challenging try is to challenge the center immediately with f6. If they wait, White will seize the initiative on the kingside first.Only after Black commits to ...f7-f6, we will play Bd3, when the kingside has been slightly weakened, and our knight is in a better position. The other point of Nd2 is that we want to arrange our knights either Steinitz-style with Ndf3-Ne2 to bolster the pawn wedge or with the king knight coming out to h3, which leaves the bishop unblocked.Which one we choose depends on how Black proceeds.} f6 $7 6. f4 {Now that Black has created the inclusion of ...f7-f6, f2-f4, White no longer has as free a hand on the kingside thanks to the pawn tension. Here, Black has a few possibilities for how they want to set up.} Nh6 {Is the other main move – Black abandons the idea of castling long, and instead opts to pivot to a castles short setup instead. However, this move essentially gives up on the idea of ...g7-g5, which means the e5-pawn is here to stay.Without a way to remove the f4-pawn, fxe5 will always be met with fxe5 with a big advantage. In fact, it is White who may choose to resolve the tension at a favorable moment.After ...Nh6, Black is not lost but will be perpetually worse.} 7. Ndf3 Be7 8. Bd3 Bxd3 {Black must initiate the capture.} (8... O-O $6 {keeping the tension is what Black would like to do, but fails concretely to} 9. Bxf5 Nxf5 $2 {, what Black would like to play.} (9... exf5 {is the lesser evil, but this is obviously not the ideal way to recapture.} 10. Ne2 {, here, White is simply much better. Black's setup does not make sense, and the position is too cramped.}) {But the issue is that we have time for:} 10. g4 Nh6 11. exf6 gxf6 12. Qe2 $1 $18 {setting up f4-f5!, which will cause a huge headache for Black. We might not want to rush with playing Qxe6+ or f4-f5-fxe6, and instead hang these threats over Black's head to force them to set up their pieces awkwardly.This knight is terrible here.}) 9. Qxd3 Nf5 10. Nh3 h5 11. O-O $14 {[%cal Gb2b4,Ga2a4,Gb4b5,Yf3d2,Yd2b3,Yb3c5] The dumb-looking knight on h3 stops all of Black's potential ideas on the kingside by locking down the h and g-pawns, and in the meanwhile, White is rushing the queenside. Potentially, we can swing the knight around to b3, since it's not needed on the kingside anymore.} *

