1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Qxd5 3. Nc3 Qd6 4. d4 Nf6 5. Nf3 a6 6. g3 Bg4 {Follow the variation here.} 7. h3 Bh5 8. Qe2 Nc6 9. Be3 O-O-O 10. Bg2 e6 11. O-O Be7 $2 {[%cal Ga1b1] Way too slow. Now White gets to coordinate with Rab1 instead, then storm the queenside..} (11... Qb4 {As we will see in the course, Black's only try is to stir up trouble with ...Qb4, to which we respond} 12. Rfb1 $16) 12. Rab1 Nd5 13. Nxd5 exd5 14. b4 {Without the queen over here to hold up the advance of the pawns, White's attack proceeds unabated.} Rhe8 15. b5 Nb8 16. c4 Bf6 17. c5 Qe6 18. Rb4 $18 {[%cal Gc5c6,Gf1c1,Gf1b1] Black tries to defend, but without any counterplay of their own, it's just a matter of time. All the rooks come to the queenside, and the files are busted open.} Bg6 19. Rc1 axb5 20. Rxb5 Qa6 21. Qb2 Bd3 22. Rb3 Nc6 23. Nd2 Ne7 24. Rcc3 Be2 25. Ra3 Qe6 26. c6 Nxc6 27. Nb3 Ba6 28. Rxa6 bxa6 29. Nc5 1-0

