1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Nf6 3. d4 Bg4 $6 4. f3 Bf5 5. g4 Bg6 6. c4 e6 7. Nc3 exd5 8. g5 Nh5 $2 (8... Nfd7 {is the more challenging, but still dubious, option.}) 9. f4 Nc6 10. Be2 {[%cal Ge2h5] Rozentalis clearly got out prepared and found himself the victim of a miniature.} Nb4 11. Bxh5 Nc2+ 12. Kf2 Nxa1 13. Bg4 {I ended the analysis around here, since most likely the knight on the corner won't survive, which means we will have a material advantage on top of an overwhelming positional advantage.To train the line, you can go to the theoretical section.} h5 14. Bh3 Bc2 $6 15. Qe2+ {White wanted to give this check anyway!} Be7 16. Nf3 dxc4 17. Qxc4 {[%csl Rf7][%cal Gf3e5,Gc4f7,Gh1e1]} Bh7 18. Ne5 {The attack is now unstoppable. The a1-knight is totally useless.} O-O 19. g6 Nc2 20. gxh7+ Kh8 21. Ne2 Bh4+ 22. Kf1 Be1 23. Qxf7 $1 {A nice way to finish the game.} Qd6 24. Bf5 Qxe5 25. Qg8+ 1-0

