1. e4 d5 2. exd5 c6 (2... e6 3. Bb5+ $1 {This strikes me as easier than taking on e6. I want to keep Black's pieces from developing too fast.}) 3. dxc6 Nxc6 4. Bc4 {[%cal Gb1c3,Gg1e2,Gd2d3] I like this move order, making sure that we don't have to worry about ...e7-e5-e4 if our knight is on e2.} Nf6 (4... e5 5. d3 {is similar.}) 5. Ne2 {[%cal Ge1g1,Gb1c3,Gd2d3] O-O comes next. Nbc3, d2-d3... I don't see any compensation for the pawn.} *

