1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Nf6 3. d4 Bg4 $6 {[%csl Rd1] The Portuguese Gambit. It's tricky, but one of the openings that we can truly 'punish' by playing accurately! White does have to memorize some lines, but you can count on a huge position if you do.} 4. f3 $1 {[%csl Gd5][%cal Gc2c4,Gc4d5,Rf3g4] The first thing to know when playing against the Portuguese is that we shoud make Black work to recoup the d5-pawn. This means that we are immediately attacking this bishop, gaining a tempo so that we can defend the pawn with c2-c4 on the next move.} Bc8 {I guess I will show ...Bc8 and ...Bd7 because they are objectively best, but they are trivial to bust and that is probably why nobody plays them.} 5. c4 c6 {[%csl Rd5]} 6. dxc6 Nxc6 7. d5 $16 {[%csl Gd5][%cal Gc6e5,Gd1d4,Gc1e3,Gb1c3] Black is not going to be fast enough to cause problems. White develops very quickly with Nc3, Qd4, and Be3, followed by long castling.} *

