1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Nf6 3. d4 Bg4 $6 {[%csl Rd1] The Portuguese Gambit. It's tricky, but one of the openings that we can truly 'punish' by playing accurately! White does have to memorize some lines, but you can count on a huge position if you do.} 4. f3 $1 {[%csl Gd5][%cal Gc2c4,Gc4d5,Rf3g4] The first thing to know when playing against the Portuguese is that we shoud make Black work to recoup the d5-pawn. This means that we are immediately attacking this bishop, gaining a tempo so that we can defend the pawn with c2-c4 on the next move.} Bd7 {The machine claims this is Black's best option. It's probably right, but also not scary at all.} 5. c4 c6 6. Nc3 $1 cxd5 7. cxd5 $16 {[%csl Gd5][%cal Gc1e3,Gf1c4,Gg1e2,Gd1b3] Black will not get back his lost pawn, and we have an easy development scheme for our pieces. Their only chance to stop us from reaching a perfect coordination with Bc4 next is to immediately play ...e7-e6, but this will not equalize either, or come close.} e6 8. dxe6 Bxe6 9. Bd3 {[%cal Gg1e2,Ge1g1] Nge2 and O-O comes next, and Black definitely does not get enough for the pawn.} *

