. Kf2 Nxd5 (14... Nxa1 15. hxg6 Nxd5 16. Qxg7 Rf8 17. gxh7 {is wraps.}) 15. hxg6 Ndb4 {[%cal Gd8d4] Black's best option here is to bail out and trade queens.} 16. Qxg7 {[%csl Rh8]} Qd4+ {But the endgame down two pawns is clearly hopeless.} 17. Qxd4 Nxd4 18. gxh7 $18 {[%csl Gg5,Gh7] So in summary, the Portuguese Gambit is a very punishable opening that relies on cheap tricks to 'get' you. But knowing the most challenging lines will lead White to a winning or almost winning position every time.} *

