1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Nf6 3. d4 Nxd5 4. c4 Nb6 $6 {[%csl Yb6][%cal Rc7c5,Gd4c5,Gc5b6] A poor square. This knight belongs on f6, where it covers the kingside and does not interfere with the c4-c5 idea.With c4-c5 being more difficult to achieve since after we take, the knight is attacked, Black's main objective is now the ...e7-e5 break. Speaking of ...e7-e5, Black is in fact threatening to play this break right now. So, unlike many similar positions, we need to develop the king knight first to prevent this.} 5. Nf3 $1 Bg4 $6 {The move that we are normally afraid of runs into...} 6. c5 $1 {[%csl Rb6]} Nd5 7. Qb3 $18 {[%cal Yg4c8,Gf1c4,Gf3e5,Gb1c3] The bishop has to run in reverse to cover the pawn. Black is busted.} *

