1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Nf6 3. d4 Nxd5 4. c4 Nb6 $6 {[%csl Yb6][%cal Rc7c5,Gd4c5,Gc5b6] A poor square. This knight belongs on f6, where it covers the kingside and does not interfere with the c4-c5 idea.With c4-c5 being more difficult to achieve since after we take, the knight is attacked, Black's main objective is now the ...e7-e5 break. Speaking of ...e7-e5, Black is in fact threatening to play this break right now. So, unlike many similar positions, we need to develop the king knight first to prevent this.} 5. Nf3 $1 g6 6. Nc3 Bg7 7. Be2 O-O 8. h3 Nc6 9. Be3 ({Don't be tempted by} 9. d5 $2 Na5 {when there will be a problem on c4.}) 9... e5 {Other moves don't make sense. We can castle and develop normally, and Black has no plan.} 10. d5 {[%csl Rc6]} Ne7 {[%csl Re5][%cal Gg7a1]} (10... Na5 $2 {Black cannot win the c4-pawn, so the knight will end up stranded on a5.} 11. Nd2 c6 12. b4 $18 {with the Black pawn on e5 instead of e7, we can play b2-b4 here. White wins a piece and the game.}) 11. g4 $1 {[%csl Gf5] Domination. Taking away the pivot point for the black minors.} f5 {Seems dangerous, but it turns out neither of Black's threatened pawn pushes is of any concern. The main thing is that we prevented a piece from occupying f5.} (11... e4 {seems like desperation to me.} 12. Nxe4 f5 13. Nc5 Bxb2 14. Ng5 $1 $18) 12. Qd2 e4 {[%csl Ge4][%cal Gc3e4]} ({▷} 12... f4 13. Bc5 $18) ({▷} 12... Nd7 13. Bg5 $18 {Black is in a total bind. From here, we can castle long and begin considering various breakthrough ideas like Qe3, Bh6, or d5-d6.}) 13. Nh4 {[%cal Ge1c1,Ge3h6,Gh4g2,Gg2f4] Against slow moves, we want to get the knight out of dodge and reroute it to f4 via g2, and then castle long, when White will have a winning kingside attack.} f4 {[%csl Rh4]} ({Black has to try} 13... Nexd5 14. Nxd5 Qxh4 $2 (14... f4 {is best and transposes back to the main line.}) 15. Bg5 {leaves the queen trapped on h4.}) 14. Bxf4 Nexd5 15. Nxd5 Nxd5 16. cxd5 Qxh4 17. Rc1 $18 {[%csl Rc7,Yc8][%cal Gf4g3,Ge1g1] White enters the middlegame with a winning position. White is going to win the c-pawn, and Black's bishop on c8 sucks.We can kick the queen on h4 via Bg3 in order to castle.} *

