1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Nf6 3. d4 Nxd5 4. c4 Nb4 $2 {We chase the knight around the board and gains tons of space for free.} 5. a3 {[%csl Rb4]} N4c6 (5... N4a6 6. Nc3 $18 {Play normal moves and White is significantly better.}) 6. d5 {[%csl Rc6]} Ne5 7. Qe2 {[%csl Re5][%cal Gb1c3,Gc1g5,Ga1d1] Paving the way for Rd1. Black's fundamental problem in these kinds of positions is that with ...e7-e6 unavailable, it's difficult to develop.} *

