1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Qxd5 3. Nc3 {First, let's get these two ridiculous queen checks out of the way. They aren't difficult to bust, as the play is very linear into bad positions for Black.} Qe5+ $6 4. Be2 Bg4 {The main idea of ...Qe5+ – Black takes steps to prevent Nf3, and thus forcibly trades the light-squared bishops, which White has been trying to avoid. However, in this case, Black loses too much time.} (4... c6 {Black will drop the queen back to c7. Technically, Black isn't losing time compared to the ...Qa5-line by doing this; the queen probably would have had to move off a5 on its own accord eventually anyway.However, Black is losing flexibility: they don't get to choose when to play ...Qc7, and thus White can set up the pieces in a more optimal configuration. In addition, this also means Black cannot get ...Bf5/...Bg4 because they are lacking that ...Be4 resource.} 5. Nf3 Qc7 6. d4 $16 {As per usual, we stick the knight on e5. This time, we have the added option of Bf4 at some point.}) 5. d4 {[%csl Re5]} Bxe2 {Black has to trade now, as the pin can't be safely maintained.} (5... Qe6 $2 6. f3 Bh5 7. g4 Bg6 8. f4 $18 {The queen and bishop come under fire. Black has to resort to playing ...f7-f5 to avoid being down a piece here.}) 6. Ngxe2 Qa5 7. O-O Nf6 {If Black had time to get ...e7-e6 and ...Nf6 in simultaneously, they would be fine. Unfortunately, they are just one tempo too slow to stabilize the position!} 8. b4 $1 {[%csl Ra5] Not allowing Black one moment of peace!} Qh5 ({▷} 8... Qf5 9. Ng3 Qg4 10. f3 {leads to something similar to the main line.}) ({▷} 8... Qxb4 $2 9. Qd3 $1 $18 {, preventing Qc4. Rb1/Nb5 is a huge threat, and Black can never play ...b7-b6 because the long diagonal will become an issue. Black is losing here, as the initiative cannot be stopped.}) 9. f3 $1 {Preventing the queen trade after Ng3. Black is once again delayed from completing development, since Nf4 is a huge threat.} Qf5 10. Ng3 $16 {White is doing fantastic. We drop one of the knights onto e4 to jack open the f-file, and are left with a lead in development and a big space advantage.} *

