1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Qxd5 3. Nc3 {First, let's get these two ridiculous queen checks out of the way. They aren't difficult to bust, as the play is very linear into bad positions for Black.} Qd8 {The most solid choice to avoid getting the queen in trouble, but also very passive.} 4. d4 Nf6 {Black can do something else on move 4, but ...Nf6 is more or less required in all of them, so I will cover all of Black's setups through the 4...Nf6 move order.} 5. Nf3 c6 6. Bc4 b5 {[%csl Rg4][%cal Gf3e5,Re5f7,Re5g4]} ({▷} 6... Bg4 $4 {Don't get Shankied.} 7. Bxf7+ $18) ({▷} 6... Bf5 7. Ne5 {transposes to 5...Bf5.}) 7. Bd3 $16 {[%csl Yc5,Rc6][%cal Gc3e4] This looks ridiculous. Black weakens the queenside for no reason.} *

