1. e4 Nf6 2. e5 Nd5 3. d4 d6 4. c4 Nb6 5. f4 dxe5 6. fxe5 Bf5 7. Nc3 e6 8. Nf3 Bb4 9. Bd3 c5 10. Bg5 Qd7 11. Bxf5 cxd4 12. Nxd4 exf5 13. Nxf5 O-O 14. O-O Qxd1 15. Raxd1 Nc6 16. Nd5 Nxd5 17. Rxd5 {White is simply a clean pawn up in this endgame. The f7-pawn is a weakness as well. On top of that, White also completely dominates the open files and is active.See the line here.} Rfe8 18. Bf4 Re6 19. a3 Bf8 20. b4 b6 21. Bg3 h5 22. h3 Rc8 23. Nd6 Rc7 24. c5 Ne7 (24... bxc5 {was the best try, but the pin is certainly unpleasant after} 25. Rxc5 {.}) 25. cxb6 $6 {The win is almost jeopardized in the next few moves, as is expected when there is such a huge difference in ratings.} axb6 26. Rb5 Ng6 27. Rxb6 h4 28. Bh2 Nxe5 29. Nc4 Rxb6 30. Nxb6 f6 31. Bxe5 fxe5 32. Nd5 Rd7 33. Rd1 Kf7 34. Kf2 Ke6 35. Ne3 Rc7 36. Rd3 Be7 37. Rb3 e4 38. a4 Rb7 39. b5 Bd8 40. Rb4 Rb8 41. Rxe4+ Kd6 42. Kf3 Ra8 43. Nf5+ Kd5 44. Nxg7 Bc7 45. Rxh4 Rf8+ 46. Ke3 Be5 47. Rg4 Rc8 48. Nf5 Rc3+ 49. Kd2 Rb3 50. Ne3+ Kc5 51. Rc4+ Kd6 52. h4 Kd7 53. g4 Bc7 54. h5 Bd8 55. Nf5 Rb2+ 56. Kd3 Bg5 57. h6 Ke6 58. Rc6+ Kd5 59. Rg6 Bf4 60. b6 Rh2 61. a5 Rh3+ 62. Ke2 Be5 63. Kd2 Rh2+ 64. Kd3 Bf4 65. b7 Rh3+ 66. Ke2 Rb3 67. Rb6 {This could have been converted a bit more cleanly, but overall was a grand effort by the underdog. He almost certainly had prepared this in advance and was able to reach the pawn-up position out of the opening!} 1-0

