1. e4 Nf6 2. e5 Nd5 3. c4 Nb6 4. d4 d6 5. f4 {[%csl Ge5]} g6 $6 {A bad plan, because the e5-pawn has been reinforced, so the g7-bishop will be ineffective.} 6. Nc3 Bg7 7. Be3 dxe5 8. dxe5 $1 {Now we see why Black should not have waited to trade. White captures symmetrically and leaves Black with a crappy position, as there is no counterplay against the d4-pawn.} Qxd1+ 9. Rxd1 $16 {[%cal Gc3b5,Gc4c5] Eventually, Black has to play ...f7-f6 or become smothered by their lack of space, which will create tons of weaknesses in their position. Among other things, Nb5 and c4-c5 are annoying ideas.} *

