1. e4 Nf6 2. e5 Nd5 3. c4 Nb6 4. d4 d6 5. f4 {[%csl Ge5]} g6 $6 {A bad plan, because the e5-pawn has been reinforced, so the g7-bishop will be ineffective.} 6. Nc3 Bg7 7. Be3 O-O 8. c5 N6d7 9. Nf3 $16 {[%csl Gc5,Gd4,Ge5,Gf4,Rg8][%cal Gh2h4] The pawn on c5 permanently prevents Black from breaking out with ...c7-c5, and thus keeps the center locked down, cramping Black severely.We can get ready to rush Harry the h-pawn with h2-h4, and h4-h5. If Black ever goes ...b7-b6, then we can play cxd6, then, when the knight can no longer go to b6.} *

