1. e4 Nf6 2. e5 Nd5 3. c4 Nb6 4. d4 d6 5. f4 {[%csl Ge5]} Bf5 {Black should not delay trading the pawns.} 6. Nc3 e6 7. Nf3 {The bishop was committed to f5 early, so we can bring out the knight before Be3 this time. Besides transposing back to the mainline, Black has three options:} Nc6 $2 8. exd6 {[%cal Rf8d6,Rc4c5,Rc5b6,Rc5d6]} cxd6 9. d5 {[%csl Rc6]} Nb4 {[%cal Bb4c2]} 10. Nd4 Be7 11. a3 {[%csl Rb4]} Na6 12. Be2 $18 {[%cal Ge1g1,Gg2g4] ...is a disaster for Black. Just make sure not to take on f5 and fix Black's structure for them.We are getting ready for O-O and g2-g4. If Black checks us on h4, we can move the king, and g2-g4 is still coming.} *

