1. e4 Nf6 2. e5 Nd5 3. c4 Nb6 4. d4 d6 5. f4 {[%csl Ge5]} Bf5 {Black should not delay trading the pawns.} 6. Nc3 e6 7. Nf3 {The bishop was committed to f5 early, so we can bring out the knight before Be3 this time. Besides transposing back to the mainline, Black has three options:} Be7 ({▷} 7... dxe5 {transposes to the mainline.}) ({▷} 7... Na6 $2 {is ridiculous,} 8. Be2 $18 {.}) 8. Bd3 $1 {This new option is available to us because there isn't pressure on d4 yet.} Bg4 (8... Bxd3 9. Qxd3 $16 {Nice and easy. Castle and the pieces come to the center.} Z0 10. Be3 {,} Z0 11. O-O {, and} Z0 12. Rad1 {will follow.}) 9. h3 $16 {[%csl Gf1][%cal Gd4e5,Ye7h4,Ye1f1] After the capture on f3, we can recapture on e5 with the d-pawn instead.} (9. h3 Bh4+ 10. Kf1 {doesn't change much.}) *

