1. e4 Nf6 2. e5 Nd5 3. c4 Nb6 4. d4 d6 5. f4 {[%csl Ge5]} dxe5 6. fxe5 {Now, ...Nc6 is surely Black's best move, and it has its own chapter. In the present section, we will examine the other options.} c5 $2 {Once upon a time this was a main move, but now it just looks bad.} 7. d5 g6 8. Bf4 {Once again, we delay the development of the g1-knight until Black cannot play ...Bg4 Either they play ...N8d7, ...e7-e6, or moves the bishop to f5. We defend the pawn with the bishop instead. The center is very secure, and Black doesn't have any means to destabilize it in the long run.} Bg7 9. Nc3 O-O 10. Qd2 $16 {[%cal Ge1c1,Gf4h6,Gh2h4] Next up, we castle and use the big center as a cover to buy time for the attack.} *

