1. e4 Nf6 2. e5 Nd5 3. c4 Nb6 4. d4 d6 5. f4 {[%csl Ge5]} dxe5 6. fxe5 {Now, ...Nc6 is surely Black's best move, and it has its own chapter. In the present section, we will examine the other options.} c5 $2 {Once upon a time this was a main move, but now it just looks bad.} 7. d5 e6 8. Nc3 {[%cal Rb6c4,Gd1a4,Ga4c4,Ga4e8] One nice point here is that Black cannot take on c4 with the hope of checking on h4, as we can respond with Qa4+ instead of taking the knight.} Qh4+ 9. g3 {[%csl Rh4]} Qd4 10. Qxd4 cxd4 11. Nb5 {[%csl Rd4][%cal Gb5c7]} Na6 12. d6 $18 {[%cal Gg1f3,Gb5d4] White will win the d4-pawn, and the game, in short order.} *

