[PlyCount "27"]
[GameId "2288537761173768"]

1. e4 Nf6 2. e5 Nd5 3. c4 Nb6 4. d4 d6 5. f4 {[%csl Ge5]} dxe5 6. fxe5 {Now, ...Nc6 is surely Black's best move, and it has its own chapter. In the present section, we will examine the other options.} c5 $2 {Once upon a time this was a main move, but now it just looks bad.} 7. d5 e6 8. Nc3 {[%cal Rb6c4,Gd1a4,Ga4c4,Ga4e8] One nice point here is that Black cannot take on c4 with the hope of checking on h4, as we can respond with Qa4+ instead of taking the knight.} exd5 9. cxd5 c4 {[%cal Rf1c4,Gd8h4] Now, don't take on c4 and walk into ...Qh4+.} 10. d6 $1 Nc6 {[%csl Re5]} 11. Nf3 $18 {[%cal Gc1f4,Gd1e2,Ge1c1] White is already winning thanks to the d6-pawn, which makes it all but impossible for Black to develop their f8-bishop. The plan is Bf4, Qe2, O-O-O.} (11. Bf4 {This move order is fine too.}) 11... Bg4 {[%csl Re5] This is the only way to even try to complicate the game, but it is not going to help.} 12. Bf4 g5 $1 {[%csl Rf4]} 13. Bg3 $1 Bg7 14. Be2 $1 {No need to fear Black taking on e5. They will be crushed on the light squares.} *

