1. e4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. Nc3 d6 4. Be3 a6 5. g4 b5 6. Bg2 Bb7 7. h4 h6 8. g5 hxg5 9. h5 {This game will illustrate how quickly the game can go south for Black once the h-file is torn open.} b4 10. Nd5 e6 11. Nxb4 {You can train this position here.} c5 $2 (11... g4 $1) ({and} 11... gxh5 {are the only moves.}) 12. hxg6 (12. dxc5 {is what I give in the course}) ({but} 12. hxg6 {is just as good.}) 12... Rxh1 13. gxf7+ Kxf7 14. Bxh1 cxb4 15. Nf3 Bh6 16. Nxg5+ $1 Bxg5 17. Qh5+ Kf8 18. Bxg5 Qe8 19. Qh2 $1 {[%cal Gh2d6,Gh2f4] Some nice geometry, targeting the soft dark squares. Qxd6+ and Qf4+ are now in the air. Black can't defend everything.} e5 20. O-O-O Nd7 21. Rd3 Ndf6 22. Rg3 $4 {An unfortunate oversight. Up until here, White was playing brilliantly.} (22. Qh8 $1 Qh5 23. Bxf6 {gets the job done.}) 22... Qh5 23. Qg1 Bxe4 24. Bxf6 Qh6+ 25. Kb1 Nxf6 $4 (25... Qxh1 26. Rxg8+ Kf7 {was a dead draw.}) 26. Bxe4 Rd8 27. Bf5 exd4 28. Rh3 Qg7 29. Qh1 Re8 30. Rg3 Qf7 31. Qh6+ Ke7 32. Rg7 Kd8 33. Rxf7 1-0

