1. e4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. Nc3 e6 $2 {A weak setup. The pawn does not belong here, and the plans it supports ...d7-d5 and ...Ne7 also do not belong with the fianchetto.White can take direct action here.} 4. h4 $1 {Pick your poison. Black can either try to stop the rush with ...h7-h6 or ...h7-h5, or ignore what we are doing.} h6 5. h5 g5 6. f4 gxf4 7. Bxf4 $18 {[%cal Yd7d6,Ye6e5,Gf4g3,Gd4d5] The one idea to keep in mind is that Black is trying to go ...d7-d6 and ...e6-e5, so once ...e6-e5 is threatened, we should pull this bishop back to g3 to meet ...e6-e5 with d4-d5. Otherwise, this position is completely busted for Black.} *

