1. e4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. Nc3 e6 $2 {A weak setup. The pawn does not belong here, and the plans it supports ...d7-d5 and ...Ne7 also do not belong with the fianchetto.White can take direct action here.} 4. h4 $1 {Pick your poison. Black can either try to stop the rush with ...h7-h6 or ...h7-h5, or ignore what we are doing.} Ne7 $2 {The worst of the three options. It turns out, the h-pawn really can't be ignored!} 5. h5 d5 6. h6 $18 {[%csl Rf8][%cal Rg7f8] White is completely winning once the bishop has to slunk back to f8.} *

