1. e4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. Nc3 e6 $2 {A weak setup. The pawn does not belong here, and the plans it supports ...d7-d5 and ...Ne7 also do not belong with the fianchetto.White can take direct action here.} 4. h4 $1 {Pick your poison. Black can either try to stop the rush with ...h7-h6 or ...h7-h5, or ignore what we are doing.} h5 5. Bg5 Ne7 6. g4 $18 {[%cal Gg4h5,Gg1e2,Ge2g3,Gh4h5] The punishment our opponent gets for playing such a questionable line. Coming up is gxh5, followed by Ne2-g3 and h4-h5, demolishing the kingside.} *

