1. e4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. Nc3 a6 $5 {Black is trying to go ...b7-b5 before ...d7-d6, which is not an entirely stupid idea. However, there are some drawbacks, which we will soon see.} 4. Be3 b5 (4... d6 {transposes back to the main line.}) 5. h4 $1 {In the main line, I recommended g2-g4, which is easier to play than h2-h4, but here we have a favorable version of the h2-h4 mainline. Because Black does not have ...d7-d6 yet, Black's main idea against what we're about to do does not work.} h6 6. h5 g5 7. f4 $1 {Opening up the position.} gxf4 8. Qg4 $1 {[%csl Rf4,Rg7] We are recapturing with the queen.} Nf6 {[%csl Rg4] Setting a clever trap, but we are much better if we don't fall for it.} 9. Qxf4 $16 ({We have successfully jacked open the kingside before Black was able to start creating counterplay. Ideas connected with e4-e5 may be possible in the near future.Don't get shankied!} 9. Qxg7 $4 Rh7 {.}) *

