1. e4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. Nc3 a6 $5 {Black is trying to go ...b7-b5 before ...d7-d6, which is not an entirely stupid idea. However, there are some drawbacks, which we will soon see.} 4. Be3 b5 (4... d6 {transposes back to the main line.}) 5. h4 $1 {In the main line, I recommended g2-g4, which is easier to play than h2-h4, but here we have a favorable version of the h2-h4 mainline. Because Black does not have ...d7-d6 yet, Black's main idea against what we're about to do does not work.} Bb7 6. h5 b4 7. Nd5 e6 8. Nxb4 Bxe4 9. f3 $16 {[%csl Re4][%cal Gd1d2,Gb4d3] Black did not gain much by capturing our center pawn. In fact, it simply eases us of the burden of having to watch over that pawn by being able to cash it in for Black's b-pawn.After the simple f2-f3, we intend to develop with usual moves like Qd2 and Nd3, and the h5-pawn is going to be a big asset in the upcoming positions.} *

