1. e4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. Nc3 a6 $5 {Black is trying to go ...b7-b5 before ...d7-d6, which is not an entirely stupid idea. However, there are some drawbacks, which we will soon see.} 4. Be3 b5 (4... d6 {transposes back to the main line.}) 5. h4 $1 {In the main line, I recommended g2-g4, which is easier to play than h2-h4, but here we have a favorable version of the h2-h4 mainline. Because Black does not have ...d7-d6 yet, Black's main idea against what we're about to do does not work.} h5 {In general, this would be the move I would want to avoid and the reason we go for g2-g4 first in the main line. But here, there is an important difference on display.} 6. Nf3 $1 {[%cal Gf3g5] Rushing to g5.} Bb7 $6 {What's been tried the majority of the time in practice. However, this move critically moves away from the g4-square.} 7. Ng5 d6 {This is a bit late.} 8. g4 $1 hxg4 9. Qxg4 Nd7 10. Qg1 $16 {[%cal Ge1c1,Gd4d5,Gf1h3,Gh4h5] Prophylaxis against ...Ngf6. After long castles, Black is too cramped, and the position has too many weaknesses.} *

