1. e4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. Nc3 d6 4. Be3 {Now, the main move, by a wide margin, is ...a7-a6, which will be covered in its own chapter. But Black has other moves they can try, too, that we must be ready for.} Nf6 {[%csl Ge3][%cal Rf2f4] With ...Nf6, Black is transposing into a Pirc, but one where White has already committed to the English attack instead of the Austrian. This is somewhat annoying because it means that we have to play something different from my main recommendation.Fortunately, there is a simple and direct way for White to play here to secure the edge.} 5. Qd2 O-O $6 {Like ...O-O in the ...a7-a6-line, this is dangerous.} 6. O-O-O {[%cal Re7e5,Bd4e5] We can prevent ...e7-e5 first before going for Bh6.} c6 7. Bh6 b5 8. f3 $16 {[%cal Gf3e4,Rb5b4,Gh2h4,Gh4h5] h4-h5 is on the way, and Black will face a vicious attack.} *

