1. e4 d6 2. d4 {There is a lot of overlap between the 2nd move Pirc sides with other lines, with many transpositions. As a result, there's not too much to cover here.} c5 $2 {A lousy move.} 3. dxc5 {[%cal Rd6c5,Rd1d8]} Qa5+ (3... dxc5 4. Qxd8+ {is terrible.}) 4. Nc3 Qxc5 5. Be3 {[%csl Rc5]} Qa5 6. Qd5 $16 {[%csl Ra5][%cal Bc3d5] Getting the queens off. Once the knight reaches d5, the king will have to move to cover the check.If the queen retreats, on the other hand, White will have an overwhelming lead in development.} *

