} 7. Nxd4 g6 8. O-O Bg7 9. Kh1 $1 {[%cal Ra7g1] Take it slow! Getting off the g1-a7 diagonal and avoiding any pin.} O-O 10. f5 Nbd7 11. Qe1 Ne5 12. Qh4 {[%csl Rd4][%cal Gc1g5,Gc1h6,Gf5g6,Gf1f8,Yd3e2,Yf6d7,Rg7d4] → From here, our attack is very straightforward. We can use the g5- and h6-squares and the f-file to create pressure against Black's position.Meanwhile, the advanced f-pawn cramps the c8-bishop. One important thing to remember is to respond to ...Nfd7 with Be2 to avoid blundering the d4-knight.} *

