1. e4 d6 2. d4 Nf6 3. Nc3 g6 4. f4 Bg7 5. Bd3 Bg4 6. Qd2 $5 {[%cal Gh2h3,Ge4e5] Stubbornly sticking to the plan of not allowing the bishop to exchange itself for the knight.Now Black has to do something while the bishop is in limbo, otherwise h2-h3 and e4-e5 will start pushing the minor pieces back.} e5 7. dxe5 dxe5 8. h3 {[%csl Rg4]} Be6 9. f5 {[%csl Re6]} gxf5 10. exf5 Bd5 11. Qe2 $14 {[%csl Ge4][%cal Gc1g5,Ge1c1] Objectively speaking, it's not so bad for Black, but the position is certainly unstable with many weaknesses. Against everything, including the ...e5-e4-pawn break, we should play Bg5 next to pin down the knight.} *

