1. e4 d6 2. d4 Nf6 3. Nc3 g6 4. f4 Bg7 5. Bd3 O-O 6. Nf3 Nbd7 7. e5 $1 {[%csl Rd7][%cal Rf6d7] A natural reaction to ...Nbd7, since the other knight will have to go to the back rank now.} Ne8 8. Qe2 c5 9. Be3 cxd4 10. Bxd4 dxe5 11. fxe5 $16 {[%csl Rc8,Rd7,Re8,Rg7] A dominating position. Black's minors are all tied up in a Gordian knot, and will take a long time to get coordinated. In the meantime, we can prepare to rush the kingside with h4-h5.If Black reroutes one of the knights to attack the bishop on d4, our response should be to defend it with Be4 instead of retreating it; trading on d4 will lose even more time to the rook recapturing with tempo.} *

