1. e4 d6 2. d4 Nf6 3. Nc3 g6 4. f4 Bg7 5. Bd3 O-O 6. Nf3 Na6 7. O-O c5 8. d5 $16 {[%cal Ga2a4,Ge4e5,Gf4f5,Gh2h3] A structure which is extremely favorable for White. Black has several follow-ups, but there are a few general principles White should keep in mind.Normally we want to play a2-a4 to stop ...b7-b5 for good, and prepare either e4-e5 or f4-f5. Make sure to control Black's counterplay and avoid unnecessary piece trades.} *

