1. e4 d6 2. d4 Nf6 3. Nc3 g6 4. f4 Bg7 5. Bd3 O-O 6. Nf3 Bg4 $6 7. h3 Bxf3 8. Qxf3 Nc6 9. Be3 e5 10. dxe5 $1 {A common response to pressure against the dark squares in the center. dxe5 removes the target on d4, followed by f4-f5, which keeps the long diagonal and e5-square closed off to the black pieces.} dxe5 11. f5 {[%csl Gf5][%cal Gg2g4,Ge1c1,Gg4g5] The position is under control, and we should prepare to continue making advances on the kingside.} *

