1. e4 d6 2. d4 Nf6 3. Nc3 g6 4. f4 Bg7 5. Bd3 O-O 6. Nf3 Nc6 7. O-O Bg4 {[%csl Rd4][%cal Ge7e5,Rg4d1] Black is ready for ...e7-e5, so it's time to make our move:} 8. e5 $1 {[%csl Rf6]} dxe5 9. dxe5 {[%csl Rf6]} Nd5 10. h3 {[%csl Rg4]} Nxc3 11. bxc3 Bf5 $14 {[%cal Gd1e2,Gf1d1,Yd3f5] From here, we have two equally good continuations: ▷ We trade on f5 and enter a better endgame with decent chances to press or, ▷ Play Qe2 and Rd1 to hold the fort on d3 and wait for Black to initiate the trade, which will fix the structure.Both are easy positions to play.} *

