1. e4 d6 2. d4 Nf6 3. Nc3 g6 4. f4 Bg7 5. Bd3 e5 (5... c6 $6 6. Nf3 $16 {, h2-h3 then e4-e5 is coming up, as always, ...c7-c6 does not belong against the three pawns setup.}) 6. dxe5 dxe5 {[%cal Yf4f5,Yg6f5,Ye4f5,Re5e4]} 7. Nf3 ({Here,} 7. f5 {is running into} gxf5 8. exf5 e4 $1 {. So instead, we must allow the capture on f4.}) 7... Bg4 $6 8. h3 {[%csl Rg4]} Bxf3 9. Qxf3 $16 {[%csl Gc1,Gd3][%cal Bf4f5] This is a favorable trade for White. The bishop pair will be strong in the open position, since I imagine Black does not want to see f4-f5 happen and will likely take on f4.} *

