[White "Caro-Kann: Introduction & Model Games"]
[Black "Ivic, Velimir vs. Bluebaum"]
[Result "1-0"]
[ECO "B15"]
[Annotator "SchackNuva"]
[PlyCount "89"]
[GameId "2288537761710498"]

1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. Nd2 dxe4 4. Nxe4 Nf6 5. Nxf6+ exf6 6. c3 Bd6 7. Bd3 O-O 8. Qc2 Re8+ 9. Ne2 h5 10. O-O h4 11. h3 Nd7 12. Bd2 Nf8 13. Rae1 {You can train the line here.} Be6 $6 {This is a poor decision. White wanted f2-f4-f5 anyway, and now it comes with tempo. Ivic put on a clinic.} 14. f4 $1 Qc7 15. f5 $1 Bd7 16. c4 $1 {Once f4-f5 is on the board, it is much easier to get c3-c4 in because you do not need to concern yourself with Ne6. Now, c4-c5 coming next would leave all of Black's pieces passive forever.} b6 (16... c5 {I would have tried this one, but Black's position is still lousy.} 17. d5 Nh7 18. Qc1 $16 {Black isn't doing much, and White can look for Nc3-e4 next.}) 17. b4 $1 {Renewing the threat.} c5 18. dxc5 bxc5 19. b5 $16 {[%cal Ge2c3,Gc3d5]} ({Long term, the queenside structure is totally winning for White, and Black is not getting nearly enough kingside chances to make up for it.Soon enough,} 19. b5 Z0 20. Nc3 {,} Z0 21. Nd5 {comes, and pieces start trading on the e-file.}) 19... Nh7 20. Nc3 Ng5 21. Nd5 Bh2+ 22. Kh1 Qd6 23. Rd1 Be5 24. Bxg5 $5 {Ivic decides the game with a direct attack. It definitely works, though it has to be said that White could have also dribbled the ball into the goal.} (24. Qc1 $5 Nh7 25. Be4 $18 {Black can barely move, and White can send the queenside pawns.}) 24... fxg5 25. f6 $1 Bd4 26. Bh7+ Kh8 27. fxg7+ Kxg7 28. Nf6 $2 {This gives Black another chance at life.} (28. Bf5 $1 {Once the light-squared bishops are off, Black won't be able to keep those light squares under control for long.}) 28... Re5 $1 29. Be4 Rh8 $1 {Now White has to win the game all over again. Still, even after missing the most direct way, Black has a tough defense ahead.} 30. Bd5 Be6 $2 (30... Bf5 $1 {This was an 'only move'. It's not that hard, but it's not totally obvious either.}) 31. Ng4 $1 Rxd5 32. cxd5 Bd7 33. Qc1 {White recovered from the error and is winning once again.} Rh5 34. Rxd4 $1 cxd4 35. Nf6 {The rest was easy.} Rh6 36. Qxg5+ Rg6 37. Nh5+ Kf8 38. Qxh4 Bxb5 39. Rb1 Bc4 40. Rc1 Ba6 41. Qxd4 Bb7 42. Qh8+ Rg8 43. Qb2 Rxg2 44. Kxg2 Bxd5+ 45. Kf1 1-0

[Event "Lifetime Repertoires: Shankland's 1.e4 – Part 1 Caro-Kann, French & Sidelines"]
[Site "?"]
