1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 dxe4 4. Nxe4 Bf5 5. Ng3 Bg6 6. h4 h6 7. Nf3 Nd7 8. h5 Bh7 9. Bd3 Bxd3 10. Qxd3 e6 11. Bd2 Ngf6 12. O-O-O Be7 13. Ne4 Nxe4 (13... Qb6 14. Nxf6+ Nxf6 15. Ne5 {This is how we would reach the position seen in the game.}) 14. Qxe4 Nf6 15. Qd3 (15. Qe2 {I gave this move in the course.}) 15... Qb6 16. Ne5 {Black's position is already very difficult, and their next move did not make it any easier.} Rf8 $2 {I suppose they wanted to castle long, but this was a bit too optimistic.} (16... Rd8 {This should have been preferred, though Black's position is still very difficult.}) 17. Qe2 $1 {No long castle for you!} Qc7 (17... O-O-O 18. Nxf7 $16) 18. Rh3 $6 (18. Rhe1 $1 {This was the way.} O-O-O 19. Nxf7 $1 Rxd4 20. Qxe6+ {Nice that the bishop is hanging on e7. Thanks Rhe1!}) 18... Bd6 (18... O-O-O {Here Black really could have castled, as d4 is loose if we take on f7. Still, their position is not fun.} 19. Rd3 $14 (19. Nxf7)) 19. Rb3 $1 {Very resourceful. Black still cannot castle long, but they cannot really hope to fight back with their king in the center either.} a5 (19... O-O-O 20. Nxc6 $1 {Black cannot take the knight without losing the queen.} Qxc6 (20... bxc6 21. Qa6+ Kd7 22. Rb7 $18) 21. Rc3) 20. a4 {No rush at all. Please move! Black cannot castle long, but what else can they even try? The position is totally lost.} Nd5 21. Qg4 {Perhaps not the most precise, but also more than enough to win the game.} (21. Rg3 $18) 21... Bxe5 22. dxe5 O-O-O 23. Qxg7 $1 Rg8 24. Qxh6 Qxe5 25. Bxa5 $2 (25. Qh7 $16 {Simply getting the queen back to a decent spot was still very good for White.}) 25... Rh8 $2 (25... b6 $1 {This would have offered much more resistance.}) 26. Qd2 $18 {Now it's all over.} Nb6 27. Bxb6 $1 {Well spotted.} Rxd2 28. Rxd2 (28. Rxd2 Z0 29. Rbd3 {comes next, and there is not a thing that Black can do about it.}) 1-0

