1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 dxe4 4. Nxe4 Bf5 5. Ng3 Bg6 6. h4 h6 7. Nf3 Nd7 8. h5 Bh7 9. Bd3 Bxd3 10. Qxd3 e6 11. Bd2 Ngf6 12. O-O-O Be7 13. Ne4 Nxe4 14. Qxe4 Nf6 15. Qe2 Qd5 16. Kb1 Qe4 17. Be3 Ng4 18. Nd2 Qf5 19. Nf1 Nf6 (19... Nxe3 {As mentioned in the course, I really think Black should take on e3. This game shows what can happen if they don't.}) 20. Bc1 $1 Qb5 21. c4 $16 {White takes all the space, and Black is in a bad way. I quite like how Alikulov played the ensuing middlegame.} Qa6 22. Rh3 $1 {[%cal Gh3g3] Not subtle. Rg3 incoming!} O-O-O (22... b5 {This looks much more natural to me, forcing White to give up the d5-square. Still, Black is clearly worse.} 23. c5 $1 {Black's knight will be very nice on d5. But the rest of his position will be awful!} (23. Rg3 $5 {This is not bad either, but it is a bit more double-edged.} bxc4 24. Rxg7 Qb5 $1 25. Rg3 Nd5 26. Nd2 $14) 23... Nd5 24. Rg3 Bf6 25. Nd2 $1 O-O-O 26. Ne4 $16 {One good piece can only do so much.}) 23. Bf4 Rd7 24. Rg3 $6 {This allowed Black to get some counterplay with ...Nd5, and they almost equalized.} (24. Be5 $16 {Black can barely move.}) 24... Nd5 25. Bc1 Nb6 26. b3 Bf6 27. Rgd3 Rhd8 28. Bb2 Qa5 $2 (28... c5 $1 {This was Black's one and only chance to change the course of the game.} 29. dxc5 $2 {This would allow Black to show the tactical point.} (29. Ng3 $10) 29... Nxc4 $1 30. Rxd7 $2 Na3+ $1 {Black wins the queen, and the game.}) 29. Bc3 $1 Qf5 30. Ng3 Qh7 31. Ne4 Be7 {And we see a key theme in the castle long positions.Black's queen often has trouble finding a square, and here, she had to go to h7 to stay safe. Fine, she won't be taken, but she is horribly sidelined, and we can go straight for the enemy king.} 32. Kb2 (32. Ba5 $1 {This was stronger. There was no need to allow Na8-c7.}) 32... Na8 33. f3 Nc7 34. Qc2 f5 35. Nc5 Rd6 {White's play was not the most precise the last couple moves, and Black is almost in time to play ...g7-g6 and get their queen into play. At this point, it's time to turn up the heat.} 36. b4 $1 b6 $2 (36... g6 {This was needed.} 37. hxg6 Qxg6 38. a4 {b4-b5 can come next, and White is a bit better, but the game goes on.}) 37. Qa4 $1 {White gives a piece, and they are totally winning. It all comes down to the misplaced queen on h7 being unable to join the defense.} a5 (37... bxc5 38. bxc5 R6d7 39. Qxa7 {Ba5 and Rb3 will end the game in short order. The queen on h7 is a total spectator.}) 38. Nb3 (38. bxa5 $1 bxc5 39. a6 $1 {This would have ended things.}) 38... f4 (38... b5 39. Qxa5 bxc4 40. Nc5 Rd5 41. R3d2 $16 {Black is in bad shape, but can still hope for a miracle.}) 39. c5 {Now it's all over.} b5 40. Qxa5 Rd5 41. Qb6 Rg5 42. R3d2 Qf5 43. Na5 Qd5 44. Nxc6 Bf6 45. Nxd8 Bxd8 46. c6 1-0

