1. O-O-O {White can castle on either side, but I prefer castling long to keep the position a bit more imbalanced.} (11. O-O Re8 12. Rae1 $14 {Black is still very solid thanks to the symmetry, but his position is quite passive, and White obviously is on the more pleasant side.}) 11... Re8 12. h4 $1 {Threatening to sacrifice on h7.} Nf8 $1 13. Qd2 Bg4 14. Rdg1 $1 {[%cal Gf3e5] The rook is awkward here for the moment, but it can always regroup later. We want to make sure that Black cannot take on f3. The machine now claims Black should play ...c6-c5, which is a move I am very happy to see.} Ne6 {This feels like the human move to me.} 15. Ne5 $1 (15. Ng5 $5 {forces ...Nf8, which a human might or might not do.} Nf8 16. f3 {.}) 15... Bd6 16. Bg5 $1 Bxe5 $1 {Not the easiest to see in advance.} 17. dxe5 Qc7 18. f3 Bh5 19. Bf5 $1 Nxg5 ({If} 19... Qxe5 {, then} 20. Bxe6 {with the idea of g2-g4.}) 20. hxg5 Qxe5 $1 {Not so easy to play chess like this.} 21. Bxh7+ Kxh7 22. Rxh5+ ({In case of} 22. Re1 {, Black plays} Qf5 23. Rxh5+ Kg6 24. Reh1 Re5 $1) *

