the possibility of bringing it to b4.} 8. Bd3 c5 $1 {Now, unfortunately we will have to castle short, but this does not mean Black is easily equalizing.} 9. O-O (9. Qe2 cxd4 10. Nxd4 {, and now we see the point of starting with ...a7-a6. The bishop reaches b4.} Bb4 $1 {We can't castle long, and Black should be fine.}) 9... Be7 $1 {Now that we have agreed to castle short, Black puts the bishop on e7. This feels way too subtle for a human to grasp.} 10. Qe2 O-O (10... cxd4 11. Nxd4 O-O 12. Rad1 {transposes to the main line.}) 11. Rad1 cxd4 12. Nxd4 Nc5 {This move looks natural from a human perspective, but it's totally wrong.} 13. Bc4 $1 {No bishop for you!} Qe8 14. b4 $1 Ncd7 15. a3 $16 {Black's pieces are horribly restricted.} *

