rse, White goes for it. Now, Black has two serious setups to consider. One is to play with} 10. h4 Be6 {here and ...f5, and the other is with} (10... Nd7 {here and ...Nf8. They are both reasonably solid, but still very dangerous for Black.})) 10... Be6 $1 11. h5 f5 $1 {Now, unfortunately, the most violent way does not work. But White can still build up an attack.} 12. Be3 Nd7 13. hxg6 $1 fxg6 14. g4 $1 ({Now and only now, we can go for it. The point is that} 14. g4 Bd5 {is not working.}) 14... Bd5 $2 15. O-O-O $1 ({When} 15. O-O-O Bxh1 {was a full rook; we were running out of steam. Now, it is just an exchange, and Black is smashed.}) 15... Bxh1 16. Rxh1 $18 (16. Rxh1 Z0 ({If Black touches the g-pawn,} 16... fxg4 {, then} 17. Bxg6 {ends things. The game is over.}) 17. gxf5 {comes next.}) *

