1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 dxe4 4. Nxe4 Bf5 ({Finally, we reach} 4... Bf5 {.}) ({I consider this to be Black's best move, even though it has been largely eclipsed by} 4... Nf6 {in recent years.}) 5. Ng3 Bg6 6. h4 h6 7. Nf3 e6 {[%cal Gc6c5,Gb8c6] Black can also try to keep more flexibility by avoiding ...Nb8-d7. This way, they can hope to play ...c7-c5 and ...Nb8-c6 instead.} 8. h5 {I like staying consistent. We play the same plan, and just have to make sure to be ready in case Black tries to play without ...Nd7.} Bh7 9. Bd3 Bxd3 10. Qxd3 Nf6 11. Bd2 {[%cal Gf8e7,Ge8g8,Gd8d5]} ({If Black wants to avoid ...Nbd7, I think their best option is} 11. Bd2 Be7 {and} 12. Z0 O-O {, hoping for} 13. Z0 Qd5 {. They can also try for an earlier c5 to get the knight to c6, but those lines feel very shaky.}) 11... Bd6 12. Ne4 $14 Nxe4 13. Qxe4 ({Black has nothing better than} 13. Qxe4 Nd7 {, transposing to the 8...Bd6 line.}) *

