1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 dxe4 4. Nxe4 Bf5 ({Finally, we reach} 4... Bf5 {.}) ({I consider this to be Black's best move, even though it has been largely eclipsed by} 4... Nf6 {in recent years.}) 5. Ng3 Bg6 6. h4 h6 7. Nf3 Nd7 (7... Nf6 8. h5 Bh7 9. Bd3 Bxd3 10. Qxd3 e6 11. Bd2) ({transposes to the} 7... e6 {lines.}) 8. h5 Bh7 9. Bd3 Bxd3 10. Qxd3 e6 11. Bd2 Ngf6 12. O-O-O a5 {Ivanchuk tried this one once. I suppose it makes some sense to try to get the bishop to b4, and gaining space on the queenside is not ridiculous. Still, it's hard to believe that Black will equalize playing a move like ...a7-a5 with their king still in the center. We can proceed along with the prescribed plan.} 13. Ne4 Nxe4 14. Qxe4 Nf6 15. Qe2 Qd5 16. c4 $1 Qe4 17. Be3 $16 {Black is in big trouble. ...a7-a5 is really out of place.} ({We can play something like} 17. Be3 Z0 18. Rh4 ({next, or even just} 18. Ne5 {.})) 17... Ng4 18. Rh4 $1 *

