1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 dxe4 4. Nxe4 Bf5 ({Finally, we reach} 4... Bf5 {.}) ({I consider this to be Black's best move, even though it has been largely eclipsed by} 4... Nf6 {in recent years.}) 5. Ng3 Bg6 6. h4 h6 7. Nf3 Nd7 (7... Nf6 8. h5 Bh7 9. Bd3 Bxd3 10. Qxd3 e6 11. Bd2) ({transposes to the} 7... e6 {lines.}) 8. h5 Bh7 9. Bd3 Bxd3 10. Qxd3 e6 11. Bd2 Ngf6 12. O-O-O Qc7 {This move is usually played with the plan of castling long. Karpov used to like this kind of thing for Black back in the day, but in modern times, I do not hold the O-O-O plans in high regard.} 13. Ne4 O-O-O (13... Nxe4 14. Qxe4 O-O-O 15. g3) ({transposes to} 13... O-O-O {.}) 14. g3 $1 {[%cal Gd2f4] White wants to go Bf4 next.} Nc5 15. Nxc5 Bxc5 16. Rh4 $1 {[%cal Gd3e2] I like this one. The point is simple- we overprotect d4, so that Qe2 can come next.} Rhe8 17. Qe2 Bd6 18. Ne5 $1 {As usual, Black has a hard time dealing with the knight on e5.} ({Not} 18. Ne5 c5 $2 {because of} 19. Nc4 $16) *

