1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 dxe4 4. Nxe4 Bf5 ({Finally, we reach} 4... Bf5 {.}) ({I consider this to be Black's best move, even though it has been largely eclipsed by} 4... Nf6 {in recent years.}) 5. Ng3 Bg6 6. h4 h6 7. Nf3 Nd7 (7... Nf6 8. h5 Bh7 9. Bd3 Bxd3 10. Qxd3 e6 11. Bd2) ({transposes to the} 7... e6 {lines.}) 8. h5 Bh7 9. Bd3 Bxd3 10. Qxd3 e6 11. Bd2 Ngf6 12. O-O-O Qc7 {This move is usually played with the plan of castling long. Karpov used to like this kind of thing for Black back in the day, but in modern times, I do not hold the O-O-O plans in high regard.} 13. Ne4 O-O-O (13... Nxe4 14. Qxe4 O-O-O 15. g3) ({transposes to} 13... O-O-O {.}) 14. g3 $1 {[%cal Gd2f4] White wants to go Bf4 next.} Nxe4 15. Qxe4 Nf6 16. Qe2 {If Black had a position like this one and had castled short instead, they would be quite happy to be playing ...c6-c5 and pressuring the center; as is, this will not happen.} Bd6 17. Kb1 Rhe8 18. Ne5 $1 {As usual, the knight on e5 proves very annoying for Black if they have castled long.} c5 19. Bc1 $1 ({It's hard for Black to move.▷ They can't take on d4,} 19. Bc1 cxd4 {, because of} ({▷} 19... Bf8 {This was my best attempt, hoping for} 20. Z0 Rxd4 {next, but it does not solve Black's problems.}) 20. Rxd4 {and} Z0 21. Rc4 {, but what else is there?}) *

