1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 dxe4 4. Nxe4 Bf5 5. Ng3 Bg6 6. h4 h6 7. Nf3 Nd7 8. h5 Bh7 9. Bd3 Bxd3 10. Qxd3 e6 11. Bd2 Ngf6 12. O-O-O Be7 {This is Black's main move in the modern era, and in my opinion, their best one by a wide margin. They plan on castling short and immediately slamming ...c6-c5, counting on being able to open the center as a means to defend against a direct kingside assault.} 13. Ne4 $5 (13. Kb1 {is the most common move here, but I think Black equalizes, and they have lots of options. They can castle immediately and play for ...c6-c5, or they can play with ...Qc7, ...Qb6, or even ...Rc8 and argue that Kb1 was not the most useful move.The whole point of putting the king on b1 is to prepare for Ng3-e4 to come next, and when Black's queen reaches d5, the a2-pawn will not be hanging. I think we can be blunt and play Ne4 right away.}) 13... O-O {It's also possible for Black to castle right away. Their point is that because our queen is specifically on d3 instead of e2, it is not as easy to throw g2-g4. That being said, it strikes me as asking for trouble, and I find it unsurprising that humans have rarely chosen this move.} 14. Nxf6+ $1 {As usual, when Black has the bishop on e7 and leaves the tension with the knights, we want to take on f6 right away and force Black to make up their mind on how to recapture.} Nxf6 ({Now we see Black's point. If we had this position with our queen on e2, they would be in huge trouble after g2-g4. As is, they are able to take on g4, and we have to be a little more circumspect. After} 14... Bxf6 $2 15. g4 $1 {,} Z0 16. g5 {comes next, and Black is smashed.}) 15. Kb1 c5 $6 16. g4 $1 {Now this works like a charm. The difference is that the possibility of dxc5 means that White will not remain a pawn down.} Nxg4 17. Qe2 $1 ({Already, Black's position is critical.} 17. Qe2 Z0 18. Rhg1 {is coming. They have only one way to keep fighting, and even then, they are still a bit worse.}) 17... cxd4 $1 18. Rhg1 d3 $1 {This is a far from obvious move.} 19. cxd3 f5 $1 {Now and only now. Since the c2-pawn has been dragged to d3, White is unable to play 19. Bxh6 to bring the d1-rook into the attack via g4.} 20. Qxe6+ Kh8 21. d4 $14 {Still, White is definitely a little better here. Black's kingside structure is shaky, and sooner or later something like Bd2-c3 and Nf3-e5 could come.} *

