1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 dxe4 4. Nxe4 Bf5 5. Ng3 Bg6 6. h4 h6 7. Nf3 Nd7 8. h5 Bh7 9. Bd3 Bxd3 10. Qxd3 e6 11. Bd2 Ngf6 12. O-O-O Be7 {This is Black's main move in the modern era, and in my opinion, their best one by a wide margin. They plan on castling short and immediately slamming ...c6-c5, counting on being able to open the center as a means to defend against a direct kingside assault.} 13. Ne4 $5 (13. Kb1 {is the most common move here, but I think Black equalizes, and they have lots of options. They can castle immediately and play for ...c6-c5, or they can play with ...Qc7, ...Qb6, or even ...Rc8 and argue that Kb1 was not the most useful move.The whole point of putting the king on b1 is to prepare for Ng3-e4 to come next, and when Black's queen reaches d5, the a2-pawn will not be hanging. I think we can be blunt and play Ne4 right away.}) 13... Qb6 {If Black wanted a ...Qb6 plan, it would have made much more sense for them to play it on the previous move.} 14. Nxf6+ Bxf6 $1 15. Be3 $1 {I like this subtle move the best. White places the bishop on a good square if Black ever wants to play ...c6-c5 or castle long, and we are always ready to play g2-g4 in case he castles short.} c5 $1 ({The machine wants this one, which feels both inhuman and a bit too optimistic.After} 15... O-O $2 16. g4 $1 $16 {, the attack is coming in a big way.}) 16. Ne5 $1 {Now Black needs a bunch of 'only moves' in a row.} cxd4 $2 {This feels very human to me, and it goes bad for Black in an amusing way.} 17. Nxd7 $1 Kxd7 18. Bxd4 Bxd4 19. Qxd4+ Qxd4 20. Rxd4+ Ke7 21. Rhd1 $1 {White is ready to slam into d7. Black must play ...Rhd8, but the pawn endgame does not offer that much relief.} Rhd8 22. Rxd8 Rxd8 23. Rxd8 Kxd8 24. Kd2 $16 {This is a very hard endgame to evaluate and play. The computer insists on +0.9 or so at high depths, which is extremely unusual for a pawn endgame. In such a simplified position, normally, it would either go to 0 or +100.I suppose it thinks that eventually White will reach a queen endgame of some kind. I don't think there is any real use in digging deep here to try to find any further truth.It is clear that White possesses the healthier majority and very good winning chances. I tried sparring with the computer and lost three times in a row with Black.} *

