1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 dxe4 4. Nxe4 Bf5 5. Ng3 Bg6 6. h4 h6 7. Nf3 Nd7 8. h5 Bh7 9. Bd3 Bxd3 10. Qxd3 e6 11. Bd2 Ngf6 12. O-O-O Be7 {This is Black's main move in the modern era, and in my opinion, their best one by a wide margin. They plan on castling short and immediately slamming ...c6-c5, counting on being able to open the center as a means to defend against a direct kingside assault.} 13. Ne4 $5 (13. Kb1 {is the most common move here, but I think Black equalizes, and they have lots of options. They can castle immediately and play for ...c6-c5, or they can play with ...Qc7, ...Qb6, or even ...Rc8 and argue that Kb1 was not the most useful move.The whole point of putting the king on b1 is to prepare for Ng3-e4 to come next, and when Black's queen reaches d5, the a2-pawn will not be hanging. I think we can be blunt and play Ne4 right away.}) 13... Nxe4 (13... Qc7 14. Nxf6+ $1 {transposes to the 12...Qc7 line.}) 14. Qxe4 Nf6 15. Qe2 Qd5 {This position is supposedly the reason Kb1 is a good prophylactic move. It's a bit annoying that we need to spend a tempo to make sure that a2 does not get captured.} 16. Kb1 O-O $5 {Black can try castling here. By doing so, they point out that we have committed to playing Kc1-b1, which would not have been the case if they had switched the move order and castled before playing ...Qd8-d5. Their position does hold together, but it feels shaky, and they will need to be more accurate than we are.} 17. Be3 $1 {We are ready for Ne5 next, and Black will not be able to play ...Qe4 in response.} (17. Ne5 Qe4 $1 {is a bit annoying. Black is on time to meet} 18. Be3 {with} (18. Qxe4 Nxe4 19. Be1 {White definitely can still press in this endgame, but I would rather not resolve the tension so soon if I can help it.}) 18... Nd5 {, and we will eventually have to enter an endgame.White can still press there, but I'd rather keep the queens on.}) 17... Ng4 18. Bc1 $1 {White is one move away from Nf3-e5 winning the game on the spot.} Rfd8 {This is Black's best move, but they will definitely still suffer.} 19. Ne5 $1 (19. a3 $5 {White can also maintain the tension if they so desire.}) 19... Nxe5 20. dxe5 Qb5 $1 {Now, sadly, since Black brought the rook to d8, we don't win on the spot by taking on b5 and invading to d7. But we definitely keep some pressure.} 21. Qxb5 cxb5 22. Be3 $14 {The pressure against the a7-pawn will be very annoying for Black to deal with. They can never play ...a7-a6 on pain of Be3-b6.} *

