1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e5 b6 5. a3 Bf8 6. Nf3 (6. Nce2 {This is the move order I give in the course, which I guess is a little more accurate since we can now meet ...c7-c5 with c2-c3. But what I did is likely to transpose.}) 6... Ne7 (6... c5 7. Ne2 {I guess in theory Black could take on d4 here and I won't be able to take back with the pawn, but White is still much better after Nexd4.}) 7. Ne2 c5 8. c3 Ba6 9. h4 $1 {Going for the kingside space.} h5 $2 {This was the wrong way to stop h4-h5, h5-h6, but Black's position was already bad. Now the g5-square will be his undoing.} (9... Nbc6 {Looked more natural to me.} 10. h5 h6 {White remains much better, but it's not quite as easy to break through if I don't have the g5-square.} 11. Rb1 $16 {I like this one, hoping for b2-b4 next. Nf5 can always be met with g4, and it is not easy for Black to continue their development.}) 10. Bg5 Qd7 11. g3 cxd4 12. cxd4 Nf5 13. Rc1 {Trying to stay flexible. It turns out that the blunt move was stronger, but this is also very bad for Black.} (13. Bh3 {My computer wants to stick with the main plan directly. I was mildly annoyed by ...Qb5 here, so I thought I might as well wait for Nc6 before committing the bishop to h3.} Qb5 14. Bxf5 $1 exf5 15. Nc3 {Apparently, White is completely winning. I was not so confident during the game; the weakened light squares felt questionable.}) 13... Nc6 14. Bh3 $1 {Now Black is missing ...Qb5.} Be7 15. Bxf5 $1 exf5 16. Bxe7 Nxe7 17. O-O ({Black is totally lost thanks to his weaknesses on the dark squares. White's plan is all too easy,} 17. O-O Z0 18. Ng5 {,} Z0 19. Re1 {,} Z0 20. Nf4 {, slam} Z0 21. e6 {.}) 17... O-O (17... f4 {I was expecting this one, but White is good every which way.My plan was to give an exchange.} 18. Nxf4 $1 Bxf1 19. e6 $1 fxe6 20. Ne5 Qd6 21. Kxf1 $18 {Black's rooks do not inspire confidence compared to my knights. Qa4+ is a big threat, and my computer wants to castle, allowing Qxh5, and then to give the exchange right back on f4. Black is very, very lost.}) 18. Ng5 $1 {Ready for Nf4 and Qxh5.} g6 {Okay fine, we can't play Nf4 now because h5 is defended. But one more preparatory move...} 19. Re1 $1 (19. Re1 Z0 20. Nf4 {and} Z0 21. e6 {will come, and Black will be crushed. He tried exchanging off the knight, but this will not help either.}) 19... Bxe2 20. Qxe2 Rfc8 21. e6 $1 fxe6 22. Qe5 $1 (22. Qe5 Z0 23. Qf6 {comes next, and Black resigned.}) 1-0

