1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Nf6 {The Steinitz is one of Black's two main tries after Nc3. In general, I think it is a more promising option for them than the Winawer because they do not lose the dark-squared bishop.} 4. e5 Ne4 $2 5. Nxe4 dxe4 6. Bc4 $16 {[%cal Gg1e2,Gc1e3,Ge1g1] White has an easy development scheme, and Black will have trouble defending the weak e4-pawn.} *

