ck might want to go ...b5-b4 next to play ...Ba6, and they can consider ...Ra7 as a way to defend along the 7th rank. White has no shortage of winning continuations, but I like a funny one.} 22. Nc5 $1 ({Very simple. I want} 22. Nc5 Z0 23. Ng5 {next, and after} f6 {and} 24. Z0 Qg7 {, I want to have Nxe6+ at the end. And there's not much Black can do about it.}) 22... f6 {What else?} 23. Qxg6+ Qg7 24. Qxg7+ Kxg7 25. Nxd4 $18 {White wins a clean pawn, and the endgame should win routinely.} *

