1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Nf6 {The Steinitz is one of Black's two main tries after Nc3. In general, I think it is a more promising option for them than the Winawer because they do not lose their dark-squared bishop.} 4. e5 Nfd7 ({Recently,} 4... Nfd7 5. Nce2 {has been gaining some popularity.} ({I even played it myself the last time I faced the Steinitz, winning a nice game against Ray Robson.However, I ultimately think the main line with} 5. f4 {is a much more testing way to play, and I was happy to have the opportunity to dig deep while writing this course.})) 5. f4 c5 {Anything else would be utterly shocking.} 6. Nf3 Nc6 7. Be3 Be7 {Back when I played the French a little, this move was very popular, and I chose it twice, against Robson and Salem, reaching good positions both games. White should be a bit careful here, but they are definitely better if they know what they are doing.} 8. Qd2 (8. Ne2 $2 {This only ever works if Black has burned a tempo on ...a7-a6 or ...b7-b6.} Qb6 9. Qc1 O-O 10. c3 f6 {Black has way too much counterplay here. A tempo is a huge deal in such a sharp position.}) 8... b6 {This is also possible. Obviously, Black is not going to be able to play ...Ba6, but their point is instead that they can maintain the c5-pawn and not have to take back with a piece. As such, it will be much harder for us to castle long.} 9. Bb5 $1 {It's important to include this one first.} (9. O-O-O $2 c4 $1 10. f5 b5 {This one is quite dangerous for White. Their attack is much slower, the f1-bishop is a moron, and the c6-knight is actually a decent piece. I'd take Black.}) 9... Qc7 10. O-O-O $1 {Now and only now, we castle long. The point is that c5-c4 is not an issue any more.} c4 $6 11. f5 $1 {Black is much slower getting ...b6-b5 in, and White will not be left with a horrible light-squared bishop. White's attack is much faster.} a6 12. Bxc6 Qxc6 13. f6 $1 {Other moves are strong, but I like being very direct and opening the game.} gxf6 14. exf6 Bd6 15. Bf4 $1 b5 16. Rde1 $16 {Black is still in big trouble on the dark squares.} *

