1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e5 Ne7 5. a3 Bxc3+ 6. bxc3 ({Now, Black nearly always plays} 6. bxc3 c5 {here, but it's worth being ready for ...b7-b6 as well.}) 6... O-O $2 {Black's third most common move is very ill-advised.} 7. Bd3 $18 {[%cal Gd1h5] This position exists with ...c7-c5 and Qd1-g4 included, and Black's position comes under a lot of pressure after a quick Qg4-h5.Now, the queen comes to h5 in one move, and Black is more or less lost.} *

