1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e5 b6 {This move is hard to take seriously, but it does have some adherents.} (4... Qd7 5. a3 Bxc3+ 6. bxc3 {The only move Black ever plays here is ...b7-b6, which transposes to the}) (4... b6 {line.}) 5. a3 Bxc3+ 6. bxc3 (6. bxc3 Ne7 {would transpose to the 6...b6 line, but Black does have two extraneous options.}) 6... Ba6 7. Bxa6 Nxa6 8. Qg4 $1 {Black is forced to make a serious concession on the kingside.} Kf8 {I know Black sometimes plays plans with ...Kf8 in the Winawer, but I never believed in them. Black's king immediately declares themself. They will reside on the part of the board we are trying to open anyway, and they lose the flexibility of castling on either side.} 9. h4 {When in doubt... play h2-h4!} Ne7 10. h5 c5 $2 {The h-pawn really could not be ignored.} 11. h6 $1 g6 12. Nh3 $18 {Black is crushed on the dark squares.} *

