s plan should be to play h4-h5 themself, and then h5-h6 if allowed.} (12. h5 {This has been the main move in the past, but I don't like it.} h6 $1 {Black stops Bg5, and now White is too slow for Qf3 and g2-g4. I guess White is still better, but the position is a lot less clean.}) 12... Nc6 $2 {This feels like a human mistake to me; Black avoids the exchange and can look for ...Na5 next. But they will be crushed.} 13. h5 $1 ({Amusingly, the machine wants} 13. h5 Ne7 {back, which I refuse to take seriously.Let's see what happens if Black continues along their merry way.}) 13... Na5 14. h6 $1 g6 15. Bf6 Rhg8 16. Nf4 $18 {[%cal Gf4h3,Gh3g5,Gf6g7]} (16. Nf4 Z0 17. Nh3 {,} Z0 18. Ng5+ {, and Bg7 will easily win the game on the kingside.}) *

