1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e5 c5 5. a3 (5. Bd2 Ne7 $1 {without dxc5 here, White's position is not so special.}) 5... Ba5 {This tricky move is better than it is given credit for. The one time I ever faced it, my opponent did equalize. But if you know just a little bit, it is nothing to be scared of. I like a thematic response.} 6. Bd2 $1 {The computer prefers other moves, but I like this for its simplicity. Bc1-d2 instead of a2-a3 is a real variation, but Black should equalize with good play. Here, we have a much improved version.} Ne7 $2 {This would be Black's best move in the analogous position without a2-a3 and ...Bb4-a5 included. Here, it fails immediately.} 7. dxc5 $16 {White wins a clean pawn. This would not be the case if Black's bishop were still on b4.} *

