1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e5 c5 5. a3 (5. Bd2 Ne7 $1 {without dxc5 here, White's position is not so special.}) 5... Bxc3+ 6. bxc3 ({Now, Black's two main moves, by a wide margin, are} 6. bxc3 Ne7 ({and} 6... Qc7 {. They can often be transposed to one another. However, they do have a couple of extraneous tries that White should definitely be aware of.})) 6... Qa5 {This move is aimed at forcing a closed structure. Black argues that if they ever play ...c5-c4, a3-a4, and Bc1-a3 will make them regret their life's decisions. So, they occupy the a4-square first, and keep ...c5-c4 as a potential idea in their back pocket.} 7. Bd2 Qa4 {This is the main move by far, and it is the most flexible. Black asks us what we want to do: ▷ If we go for some Qd1-g4, they will hope to open the game quickly, while we waste time with the queen.  ▷ And if we instead aim to maximize development and give up on Qg4, Black can feel more comfortable locking the position with ...c5-c4.} 8. h4 {I like slamming ahead with the h-pawn, consistent with the overall idea. We want to play a h2-h4 and h4-h5 plan if Black hits the center early with ...c7-c5.In this particular case, Qd1-g4 becomes a very good move if Black ever takes on d4, but it is not quite as convincing if they maintain the tension instead. So, while we generally can meet ...cxd4 with Qg4, we hold off for the moment.} (8. Qg4 {I am not recommending this move, and it is important to understand why.} Kf8 9. h4 Nc6 10. h5 h6 11. Z0 Nxe5 ({is a threat,} 11... Qxc2 {is a threat, and things are going wrong. But what Black does NOT want to do is ...cxd4. We will always have Nf3 in response. Here, though, it's not so easy to keep up the initiative, and the machine is recommending Qd1 back. I can't bring myself to play like that.})) 8... cxd4 $2 {This is way too optimistic for Black.} 9. Qg4 $1 {White wins the pawn back right away. They do not even need to take on d4; it is not going anywhere.} Kf8 (9... g6 10. h5 $1 {Black immediately collapses on the kingside.}) 10. Bd3 $18 ({The cleanest, saving c2. Next up is} 10. Bd3 Z0 11. Nf3 {, and Black is cooked.}) *

