ck's best plan against Qg4 is not to play ...b7-b6, but rather to pressure the center immediately with ...Nc6.} Kf8 (9... g6 10. h5 $1 {As usual, this is huge for White.}) 10. Rh3 $1 {[%cal Gh3f3,Gh3g3]} ({I like this move, making sure that we can meet} 10. Rh3 Qxc2 {with} 11. Bd3 {. The rook can lift to f3 or g3, and Black will face a very dangerous attack in the coming moves.}) *

