es a huge problem for Black.} h6 {This position is the most critical one in the ...Qa5-a4 line. I think White is better, but they should be careful and show a good understanding.} 10. Nf3 {At long last, it is time to develop normally. If Black closes the position with ...c5-c4, we do not have Qg4 anymore. But the pawn on h5 gives White a lot more kingside potential than they might otherwise have.} c4 11. g4 $1 Bd7 12. Nh4 $1 ({Black's position is tough. They cannot rely on} 12. Nh4 f6 {for counterplay because of the weakened g6-square, and White has a clear plan for future progress.We play} 13. Be2 {, bring the queen to b2, and we might even castle long to play with Rdf1 and f2-f4, f4-f5. Unlike a lot of the similar locked structures, there is a clear plan of action here.}) *

